    "narrative": "The Austin Waves roster is anchored today by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (66.01) and **Coby Mayo** (66.72), both of whom benefit from a favorable matchup against the left-handed McClanahan. **Coby Mayo** earns the highest score of the day, buoyed significantly by a 16% park factor boost and a strong platoon advantage, while **Gunnar Henderson** (64.35) remains an elite start in that same game despite a slight downward adjustment for the L/L matchup. We are also monitoring **Liam Hicks** (59.93), whose high score is driven by a favorable matchup against Young and a notable recency boost; he is currently our most efficient option to exploit a soft SP_xERA of 4.52.\n\nStrategic benching remains a tight margin for the Waves, with **Heliot Ramos** (46.35) presenting the most compelling case for inclusion. Ultimately, **Heliot Ramos** fell just short of our OF/UTIL thresholds, as the lineup depth provided by **Jackson Merrill** (58.98) and **Kyle Tucker** (58.12) offers higher daily floor efficiency. While **Heliot Ramos** has intriguing stolen base potential against a pitcher with a slow delivery, he was passed over in favor of players with more favorable order positioning or stronger raw projections against their respective targets.\n\nWe are proceeding with caution regarding **Drake Baldwin** (46.61) and **Nasim Nunez** (47.64), both of whom face high-level pitching efficiency from Henderson and P\u00e9rez. **Drake Baldwin** in particular faces a tough test against a 2.90 xERA arm, and while his leadoff spot provides some security, his fantasy output remains volatile today. Given that Stolen Bases are our scarcest category, we are leaning heavily on our established starters, though we must keep a close eye on the late-game defensive substitutions that could impact **Nasim Nunez** and **Luis Lara** if the scores drift toward blowouts.",
